---
title: Greek sheet-pan chicken with lemon and potatoes
servings: 4
tags: [greek, chicken, sheet-pan]
cuisine: greek
time: 1 hour 10 minutes
source: Greek Sheet Pan Chicken with Lemon and Potatoes by George Zikos, Mediterranean Living, https://www.mediterraneanliving.com/greek-sheet-pan-chicken-with-lemon-and-potatoes
nutrition:
  calories: 579 kcal
  fat: 33 g
  saturated fat: 7 g
  carbohydrates: 51 g
  sugar: 4 g
  protein: 24 g
  fiber: 9 g
  sodium: 728 mg
---

Heat the oven to 400°F.

Rub the @chicken thighs{4}(skin-on) with a little @extra virgin olive oil{}, @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

In a bowl, toss the @potatoes{2%lb}(washed, in 1-inch pieces) with @salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{3/4%tsp}, the juice of @lemon{1}, @dried oregano{2%tbsp}, @dried thyme{1 1/2%tsp}, @garlic{3%cloves}(chopped), @water{1/2%cup}, @dijon mustard{1%tbsp} and @extra virgin olive oil{1/4%cup}.

Spread the potatoes on a #sheet pan{}. Tuck the @lemons{2}(halved) cut side up among them and lay the chicken on top.

Bake ~{60%minutes}, until the potatoes are tender and the chicken reads 165°F. Rest ~{5%minutes} before serving.
